# Use the Excalidraw Design System

When creating or editing any mockup, prototype, screen, or component in Figma, build
from the **Excalidraw Design System** library — do not invent components or hardcode
values when a design-system equivalent exists.

- Library file: https://www.figma.com/design/28waEFLbMoPxxQCw76guTq/Excalidraw-Design-System
  (`fileKey: 28waEFLbMoPxxQCw76guTq`).
- Before assembling anything, call `search_design_system` (and `get_libraries`) to find
  existing components, variables, and styles, and reuse them.
- Bind colors, spacing, radius, and typography to design-system **variables/tokens**
  rather than raw hex or pixel values.
- Compose screens from existing components; only create new components when the system
  has no equivalent, and match its variant/state and token conventions.
- Follow the `figma-generate-design` / `figma-generate-library` skills for the workflow,
  and `figma-use` before any `use_figma` write.

If a needed component is missing from the library, flag it rather than silently
diverging from the system.
